---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Majorelle",
  servesCuisine: ["French", "Mediterranean"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-212-935-2888",
  url: "https://www.lowellhotel.com",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "28 E 63rd St",
    addressLocality: "New York",
    addressRegion: "NY",
    postalCode: "10065",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "French restaurant inside The Lowell hotel on the Upper East Side — prix fixe fine dining, afternoon tea, and old-world service.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Majorelle Menu Guide — The Lowell, Prices, French NYC"
  description="Independent guide to Majorelle at The Lowell hotel: the $135–$155 prix fixe, French menu highlights, afternoon tea hours, and visiting tips. Prices from the restaurant's published menu."
  path="/majorelle-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/majorelle.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/majorelle.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a chic French restaurant dining room with brass and mirrors — an artist's interpretation, not the actual Majorelle"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Upper East Side · The Lowell
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Majorelle — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Inside The Lowell at 28 East 63rd Street — the discreet Upper East Side hotel beloved by
      fashion week regulars — Majorelle serves French fine dining in the classic style: a prix
      fixe menu, a proper cheese-and-sauce vocabulary, and service that remembers your name.
      (OpenTable named it one of America's Top 100 Hotel Restaurants for 2026.) Below is our
      independent walkthrough of the menu structure, reported prices, and how to plan the visit.
      Everything is written in our own words; prices are reported figures, not a copy of the
      restaurant's menu.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">28 E 63rd St, New York, NY 10065 (inside The Lowell)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">French with Mediterranean touches</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Prix fixe reported: 2 courses $135, 3 courses $155</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Dinner hours</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Reported: Mon–Sat 5–10:30pm; bar Tue–Sat 12–11pm, Sun 1–8pm</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Afternoon tea</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Reported: Wed–Sat 12–4:30pm, Sun 1–6pm (prices unverified)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Dress &amp; contact</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Jacket preferred · +1 (212) 935-2888</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>The prix fixe — $135 / $155</h2>
      <p>
        Dinner runs as a <strong>prix fixe: two courses reported at $135, three courses at
        $155</strong> (figures from the restaurant's published Fall 2023 menu — the structure holds,
        but confirm current pricing when you book). The menu reads like a love letter to classic
        French technique, with a few Mediterranean turns. Here's what the lineup has included:
      </p>

      <h2>Appetizers</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Dish</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Part of prix fixe</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Salade Majorelle — watercress, avocado, haricots verts, lemon vinaigrette</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Burrata "anchoïade" — roasted peppers, anchovy dressing</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Salade de betteraves et ricotta — beets, ricotta, mustard vinaigrette</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">"Crudo" de hamachi — jalapeños, pink peppercorn</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Poulpe grillé "méditerranéenne" — grilled octopus, pearl onions, Taggiasca olives</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Noix de Saint-Jacques — scallops with lentils and chanterelles</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Vol-au-vent d'escargots en persillade — snails in puff pastry, parsley-garlic</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Foie gras sauté with fig compote and brioche</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Main courses</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Dish</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Part of prix fixe</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Fettuccine "maison" au homard — homemade pasta with lobster</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Ris de veau aux châtaignes et morilles — sweetbreads, chestnuts, morels</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Magret de canard aux cèpes — duck breast with porcini</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Carré d'agneau rôti — rack of lamb, Swiss chard gratin Mornay</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Filet mignon de boeuf, sauce au poivre</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Saumon mariné et poché sur ratatouille — double-cooked salmon</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Cabillaud confit au vin blanc — cod with white wine, brussels sprouts</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Risotto au safran et ossobuco — saffron risotto with ossobuco</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Poulet rôti grand-mère — roast chicken, potato, mushroom, bacon</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Loup de mer grillé, sauce vierge (for two) — grilled branzino</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Sole grillée with haricots verts and mustard sauce</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">+$22 supplement</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Ossetra caviar and blini</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$265</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Sides run <strong>$15</strong> — vegetable tajine with couscous, creamed spinach, potato
        mousseline, brussels sprouts, hand-cut fries. Our take: the fettuccine au homard is the
        dish to build the meal around, and the three-course prix fixe is the right call — this is a
        room that rewards the full arc.
      </p>

      <h2>Afternoon tea</h2>
      <p>
        Majorelle also serves afternoon tea — reported hours <strong>Wednesday–Saturday 12–4:30pm
        and Sunday 1–6pm</strong>. It's a quieter, lovely way into the room. We could not verify
        current tea prices from public sources at the time of writing, so call ahead for the menu
        and pricing before planning around it.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To start:</strong> the vol-au-vent d'escargots — snails in puff pastry is peak old-school French, and this room does it straight.</li>
        <li><strong>The main:</strong> fettuccine "maison" au homard. Handmade pasta with lobster in a room like this is the whole point.</li>
        <li><strong>The classicist's pick:</strong> ris de veau — sweetbreads with chestnuts and morels for the adventurous.</li>
        <li><strong>Format:</strong> three courses. Two courses here feels like leaving early.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Jackets preferred.</strong> This is one of the few rooms left where that still means something — dress accordingly.</li>
        <li><strong>Confirm the prix fixe price</strong> when booking; the $135/$155 figures come from the published Fall 2023 menu and may have moved.</li>
        <li><strong>The Lowell bar</strong> (open longer hours than the dining room) is an excellent pre-dinner drink spot.</li>
        <li><strong>63rd Street is quiet</strong> — it's a five-minute walk from the bustle of Fifth Avenue, which is exactly the appeal.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        The prix fixe figures above (<strong>$135 for two courses, $155 for three</strong>) are from
        the restaurant's <strong>published Fall 2023 menu</strong> — the most recent detailed menu we
        could verify from public sources. Menus and prices change; afternoon tea prices could not be
        verified. Always confirm current prices with the restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
